Dark mode

Add a complete dark mode to Elowen.

The theme system must support:

* Light mode
* Dark mode
* Automatic persistence of the user’s selected theme

Place a theme toggle in a consistent, easy-to-access location such as the site header.

Use:

* A sun icon to represent light mode
* A croissant icon to represent dark mode

Do not use emoji characters for either icon. Use clean SVG icons that visually match the rest of Elowen’s interface.

The croissant icon should be simple, recognizable, and styled consistently with the sun icon rather than looking cartoonish.

Theme behavior

When the user changes the theme:

* Switch themes immediately without reloading the page
* Save the preference locally
* Preserve the selected theme across page reloads
* Preserve the selected theme when navigating between Elowen pages
* Include the selected theme in Elowen data exports where appropriate
* Restore the theme when importing an Elowen backup

If the user has never manually selected a theme, Elowen may initially respect the operating system/browser prefers-color-scheme setting.

Once the user explicitly chooses a theme, their choice should take priority.

Prevent an incorrect-theme flash while the page is loading whenever reasonably possible.

Dark mode design

Do not simply invert the existing colors.

Create a deliberate dark version of the Elowen palette that preserves the same warm, natural visual identity.

The dark theme should use:

* Deep warm neutral backgrounds
* Slightly lighter elevated surfaces
* Warm taupe interactive elements
* Soft beige or sand-colored text where appropriate
* Warm brown-gray icons
* Subtle borders with sufficient contrast
* A distinct but restrained hover state
* A very subtle lighter press state

Avoid:

* Pure black backgrounds
* Pure white text unless necessary for accessibility
* Neon colors
* Blue-tinted generic dark-mode colors
* Excessive contrast
* Glowing UI elements

All components must support both themes, including:

* Header
* Navigation
* Home page
* Search bar
* Tool cards
* Calculator
* Calculator display
* Calculator buttons
* Scientific controls
* History
* Settings/data management
* Notifications
* Dialogs
* Privacy Policy
* Terms and Conditions
* 404 page
* Footer

Use CSS custom properties for theming rather than duplicating large amounts of CSS.

A structure similar to this is encouraged:

:root {
  /* Light theme variables */
}
[data-theme="dark"] {
  /* Dark theme overrides */
}

Ensure both light and dark themes meet accessibility contrast requirements.

The theme toggle must also be keyboard accessible and have an appropriate accessible label such as:

* Switch to dark mode
* Switch to light mode

The visible icon should update to clearly communicate the relevant theme state/action.

Use subtle transitions between theme colors, but respect prefers-reduced-motion.
